<div class="note">A decree of nullity operates differently from divorce: the marriage is treated as never having validly existed. Parties facing identity or religion-based nullity claims should assemble their earliest official records — birth certificates, primary school registers, parental documents — because later-created or self-serving documents carry little weight against a consistent official paper trail.</div>
